---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { centers } from '../../lib/centers';
const path = '/jewish-life-on-campus/choosing-a-college/';
const sorted = [...centers].sort((a, b) => a.primaryCampus.name.localeCompare(b.primaryCampus.name));
---
<Guide
  title="Choosing a college with Jewish life"
  metaTitle="Choosing a College With Jewish Life: A Guide for Jewish Students"
  description="How to choose a college with strong Jewish life: questions to ask, what to look for on a campus visit, and how to find the Chabad House at Florida universities."
  path={path}
  lead="What to look for, and what to ask on a campus visit."
  image="friends-outdoors"
  imageAlt="Three Jewish college students standing together outside a Chabad House"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Jewish Life on Campus', href: '/jewish-life-on-campus/' }, { name: 'Choosing a College', href: path }]}
>
  <p>Rankings and campus tours will tell you plenty about academics and dorms, but very little about what it will feel like to be Jewish on that campus on a Friday night in October. What matters most is the people: a warm Chabad House and friends to share Shabbat with.</p>

  <h2>What to look for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>An active Chabad House.</strong> Is there a rabbi and rebbetzin who live near campus and know students by name?</li>
    <li><strong>Shabbat and holidays.</strong> Are there Shabbat dinners every week? High Holiday services? A sukkah and a Passover Seder?</li>
    <li><strong>Kosher food.</strong> If you keep kosher, what exactly is available on weekdays, on Shabbat and on Passover?</li>
    <li><strong>Learning and growth.</strong> Are there classes, fellowships like <a href="/programs/sinai-scholars/">Sinai Scholars</a>, or courses on <a href="/programs/jewishu/">JewishU</a>?</li>
    <li><strong>How Jewish students feel on campus.</strong> Ask current students directly, and ask how the university responds when problems arise.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Questions to ask on a campus visit</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Can I visit the Chabad House and meet the rabbi and rebbetzin while I'm here? (Most are happy to host visiting students and families, especially for Shabbat.)</li>
    <li>How many students come to a typical Shabbat dinner?</li>
    <li>Where do students keep kosher, and what happens on Passover?</li>
    <li>What do Jewish students do on the High Holidays when they fall during classes?</li>
    <li>What Jewish programs, trips and classes are offered each year?</li>
    <li>What is the relationship between the Jewish community and the university administration?</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Chabad at every Florida school on your list</h2>
  <p>Every one of these Florida colleges has a Chabad on Campus center ready to welcome you. Visit the page for each school to meet the rabbi and rebbetzin, see what they offer and get in touch.</p>
  <ul class="cols">
    {sorted.map((c) => <li><a href={c.url}>Chabad at {c.primaryCampus.name}</a></li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Once you've decided</h2>
  <p>Reach out to the Chabad House at your new school over the summer. Introducing yourself early means you will have a familiar face at orientation and a seat at the first Shabbat dinner of the year. Parents can do the same: see <a href="/parents/">resources for parents of Jewish college students</a>. For an overview of the whole state, read <a href="/jewish-life-on-campus/florida/">Jewish life at Florida colleges</a>.</p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .cols { columns: 2; column-gap: 40px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .cols { columns: 1; } }
</style>
